# PNEUMA: Privacy Policy and Support

Developer: Stefan Almqvist (AppLand)

App: PNEUMA

Last updated: 2026-11-01

Contact: pneuma@applandapps.com

## Privacy Policy

### Short version

PNEUMA does not collect, store, or transmit any personal data. There are no accounts, no analytics, no advertising, and no third-party tracking. Everything you make stays on your device.

### What we collect

Nothing. PNEUMA does not collect personal information, usage data, device identifiers, or location. There are no servers behind the app, and it does not send your data anywhere.

### Microphone

PNEUMA can record sound through your device microphone so you can use your own voice or surroundings as source material. Microphone access is used only while you are actively recording, and only after you grant permission. Recorded audio is written to local storage on your device and is never uploaded or shared by the app. You can deny or revoke microphone access at any time in the Settings app, in which case recording is simply unavailable. You can still import sounds.

### Motion

PNEUMA reads your device's motion sensors so that tilting it can shape the sound. The tilt is used live, while you play, and is never stored or sent anywhere.

### Bluetooth

PNEUMA uses Bluetooth only to connect wireless MIDI keyboards and controllers, and only when you pair one from MIDI settings. It does not collect information about your Bluetooth devices.

### MIDI and your local network

PNEUMA receives MIDI from keyboards connected by USB or Bluetooth, from other apps on the same device, and, if you connect to a network MIDI session over Wi-Fi, from devices on your local network. iOS may ask for permission to find devices on your local network. MIDI is used only to play sound and is never stored or sent to the internet. MIDI files you open are read on your device.

### Your audio and configs

Sounds you record or import, configs you save (with their loops and MIDI files), and WAV recordings you make all stay on your device, and in your own iCloud or Files backups if you choose to save them there. Configs are kept in a folder on your device that the app shares only with its own Audio Unit plugin, so a config you save in the app can be opened in the plugin. PNEUMA has no server and cannot see or retrieve any of this content. A WAV recording leaves your device only if you share it yourself from the share sheet.

### The Audio Unit plugin

PNEUMA includes an Audio Unit (AUv3) instrument that runs inside music apps such as GarageBand, Logic Pro, AUM and Cubasis. When you use it there, the sounds and settings you load are saved inside that music app's project, on your device or wherever that app stores its projects. The plugin collects no data either.

### Purchase

PNEUMA is a paid app with a one-time price. The purchase is handled entirely by Apple through the App Store. PNEUMA has no in-app purchases and never sees or stores your payment information. Apple's handling of your purchase is governed by the Apple Privacy Policy.

### No tracking or advertising

PNEUMA contains no advertising, no analytics or measurement SDKs, and no third-party trackers. It does not use the Advertising Identifier (IDFA) and does not request permission to track you across apps or websites.

### Children

PNEUMA does not collect data from anyone, including children. It is not directed at children under 13. Keep the volume at a comfortable level, especially with headphones.

### Data retention and deletion

All of your content lives only on your device, so you are in full control of it. Deleting a recording or config in the app removes it. Deleting the app removes all of its local data, including its configs. Sounds the plugin saved inside a music app's project stay there until you delete them in that app.

### Third parties

The only third party involved is Apple, which distributes the app. PNEUMA integrates no other third-party services.

### Changes to this policy

If this policy changes, the updated version is posted at this URL with a new Last updated date. Material changes are also noted in the app release notes.

