## Support and FAQ

Need help, found a bug, or have a feature request? Email pneuma@applandapps.com and include your device model and iOS version so we can help faster. We aim to reply within a few business days.

The info button (i) in the app explains every control.

### I do not hear anything

Check these in order:
1. Turn up the volume and make sure the device is not muted.
2. Load or record a sound first. PNEUMA plays sounds you give it, so with nothing loaded there is little to hear.
3. Touch and move on the pad. Sound is made as you play.
4. If the pause button is lit, tap it to resume.
5. If you are recording, check that you granted microphone permission in Settings, PNEUMA, Microphone.

### How do I get a sound into the app?

Tap the mic in the middle of the bottom bar to record into a slot, and tap it again to stop. Or tap an empty slot (X1 to X4) at the top to import an audio file. You can load up to four sounds, one per slot. You can also open an audio file in PNEUMA from the Files app or another app's share sheet.

### How do I record my own voice?

Grant microphone permission when asked, or later in Settings, PNEUMA, Microphone. Tap the mic, make your sound, and tap the mic again. It becomes a sound you play on the pad.

### How do I export what I make?

Tap the cassette button, right of the mic, to record everything you hear. Tap it again to stop. PNEUMA saves a 24-bit WAV file and opens the share sheet, so you can save it to Files or send it to another app.

### How do I save my setup?

Tap SAVE to keep all four slots, their sounds and settings, and your loop or MIDI file as a config. You can keep up to 12 configs. Tap OPEN to load one.

### Is there anything to unlock?

No. PNEUMA is a one-time purchase with everything included. There are no subscriptions and no in-app purchases.

### I got a new device or reinstalled PNEUMA

Download PNEUMA again from the App Store with the same Apple ID. You will not be charged again. Your configs and recordings live on the device, so they come back only if you restore a backup of that device.

### How do I connect a MIDI keyboard?

Plug in a USB MIDI keyboard, or pair a Bluetooth MIDI keyboard from MIDI settings (the keys button at the top). You can also connect over Wi-Fi with network MIDI, or play PNEUMA from another app. MIDI settings also show the full MIDI map, including MPE.

### How do loops and MIDI files work?

Tap LOOP at the bottom left of the pad and play. Tap again to close the loop. It keeps playing while you play over it. Loops can be up to a minute long. Tap MIDI, next to LOOP, to open a MIDI file (.mid), which then plays your loaded sounds. Press and hold LOOP to record a new loop, or to pick a part of the MIDI file and set its speed.

### How do I use PNEUMA in my music app?

PNEUMA is also an Audio Unit (AUv3) instrument, installed together with the app. Open PNEUMA once after installing or updating, then add it as an instrument in your music app. For example, in GarageBand: new song, swipe to External, Audio Unit Extensions, PNEUMA. In AUM, Logic Pro for iPad, Cubasis and Loopy Pro, look for PNEUMA or AppLand under Audio Unit instruments.

### PNEUMA does not show up in my music app

Open PNEUMA once, close the music app completely (swipe it away) and open it again. If it is still missing, restart the device.

### Can I use PNEUMA on my Mac?

Yes, on a Mac with Apple silicon (M1 or later). Get PNEUMA from the Mac App Store with the same Apple ID: it is the same purchase. Open it once. PNEUMA then works as an instrument in Logic Pro, GarageBand, MainStage, Ableton Live (11.3 or later) and REAPER. Cubase, Pro Tools and Bitwig Studio cannot load Audio Units from App Store apps, and PNEUMA does not run on Intel Macs or Windows.

### Does PNEUMA work offline?

Yes. PNEUMA runs entirely on the device and needs no internet connection.

### Does PNEUMA collect my data or send my recordings anywhere?

No. See the Privacy Policy above. Nothing is collected, and your audio never leaves your device unless you choose to export and share it yourself.

